From: ScarlettMac <scarlettmac@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:39:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] shader: prototype explicit LOD for the AGX
 get_num_mip_levels failure

D3DMetal on AGX M1 fails one mesh pipeline with 'Encountered unlowered
function call to air.get_num_mip_levels_' (mesh 4ee6e34d + pixel a0f0a3c9).
Its calculateLod lowering asks the texture for its mip count. With
VICTORY_PS_LOD_EXPLICIT=1 a 2D pixel shader's image_get_lod computes the
level itself: 0.5 log2 of the longer coarse-derivative length in level-0
texels, from getDimensions(h, 0), clamped to 0..15. The two result
channels keep their meaning (clamped, unclamped). Cubes, 3D, a16 and other
stages keep calculateLod. Off by default; the switch is part of the shader
cache key. Host tests pass.

Whether this is the op behind the AGX error still needs the failing
container (VICTORY_SPILL_ONLY) to confirm; it is the lower-risk half of
the getDimensions/calculateLod pair.
